Difference B/n git revert and git reset ? 

Git Reset / git Revert - Undo mistakes / commit 

git Revert creates a new commit . Git revert is useful if we want to undo changes and keep changes in git 



git reset --soft HEAD~1 [ changes are saved ] 
git status 
git reset --hard HEAD~1 [ changes are not saved ] 


In order to undo changes , we  can either use git revert or git reset. 

When we want to undo the change and keep those changes in the git history. git Revert creates a new commit 
$ git revert 8ad5d 

When we want to undo the change , and the change will be in the staging area [ git status ] 
Git reset --soft HEAD~1 

When we want to undo the change , the change will be deleted 
Git reset --hard HEAD~1 
Summary
Command	Description	Example
git revert <commit>	Creates a new commit that reverses changes while preserving commit history.	$ git revert 8ad5d
git reset --soft HEAD~1	Moves the branch pointer back one commit, keeping changes in the staging area for review.	$ git reset --soft HEAD~1
git reset --hard HEAD~1	Moves the branch pointer back one commit and discards all changes in the working directory.	$ git reset --hard HEAD~1

